#
# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions.
# Reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
#
# The shared scan workflow discovers this file at the repository root and
# passes it to trivy as --ignorefile. A config-file `ignorefile:` key in
# .github/scan_tools_configs/trivy.yml would NOT work: trivy resolves that
# against its own working directory, which is the directory above the scanned
# checkout.
#
# This is trivy's plain-text format, which takes bare check IDs and so disables
# a check everywhere. Only checks that no manifest in this repository could
# reasonably satisfy belong here. Anything that is wrong for one file but worth
# catching in another stays out, and is handled per file by `scan.skip-files`
# in .github/scan_tools_configs/trivy.yml instead.

# Root filesystem is not read-only. Every GPU workload this repository ships or
# demonstrates needs a writable root: ROCm framework containers write JIT and
# kernel caches (MIOpen, Triton, Keras), the KMM driver build/worker writes
# module artifacts, and the device/config-manager daemonsets write runtime
# state. Enabling it would need a writable emptyDir per cache path -- a set that
# differs per framework and image tag, and that no CI here can validate on GPU
# hardware.
AVD-KSV-0014

# Privileged containers. GPU device access (/dev/kfd, /dev/dri) and the sysfs
# reads the config-manager daemonset, node-problem-detector, and test-runner
# jobs perform have no non-privileged equivalent on this hardware.
AVD-KSV-0017

# Disallowed (hostPath) volumes. The same GPU workloads mount host paths to
# reach the devices, the ROCm/driver install tree, and node sysfs; the NFD
# worker mounts the host to discover features.
AVD-KSV-0121

# The four checks below fire on resources rendered from vendored third-party
# Helm subcharts (node-feature-discovery, kmm) and the node-remediation
# controller. trivy reports them against the subchart template path, but its
# skip-files mechanism cannot exclude a resource rendered from a Helm *subchart*
# (it only matches the parent chart's own templates), so a per-file suppression
# in trivy.yml is impossible and the check must be disabled repository-wide.

# Manage secrets (RBAC). The operator reconciles image-pull and webhook TLS
# secrets; the KMM subchart and the node-remediation controller read per-node
# credentials. Required grants, generated from upstream / kubebuilder markers.
AVD-KSV-0041

# Privilege escalation from node proxy. Configured by the upstream
# node-feature-discovery subchart's RBAC, not by this repository.
AVD-KSV-0047

# Exec into pods. The node-remediation controller execs into GPU workloads to
# drain and recover them -- its core function.
AVD-KSV-0053

# Default security context. The remaining occurrences are in the vendored
# upstream node-feature-discovery subchart (master / worker / gc), which sets
# its own securityContext. The operator's own shipped manifests set explicit
# security contexts and already pass this check.
AVD-KSV-0118

# --- Vulnerabilities ---

# jupyter-core uncontrolled search path (docs/sphinx/requirements.txt, a
# pip-compile lockfile; jupyter-core is a transitive Sphinx/MyST docs dep).
# The vulnerability is Windows-only -- "Jupyter Core on Windows Has
# Uncontrolled Search Path Element" -- and these docs build exclusively on
# Linux CI, so it is not exploitable here. A VEX-style not-affected suppression
# per trivy's own guidance; revisit when the docs lockfile is next regenerated
# (fixed in jupyter-core 5.8.1).
CVE-2025-30167

# --- Misconfigurations (continued) ---

# Image runs as root. Every Dockerfile here is a build, test-runner, bundle, or
# utility image that needs root to compile, install packages, or assemble the
# operator bundle -- none is a long-running service. (The shipped operator
# runtime image already sets a non-root USER and is not affected.) The
# Dockerfile scanner only honours an inline #trivy:ignore when a USER line
# exists to anchor it; these images set no USER at all, so the finding is
# file-level and can only be suppressed repository-wide.
AVD-DS-0002
